{
  "file_name": "67a32524-11.pdf",
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_index": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "o6x9afdKie",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08469055374592833,
            "y": 0.08255033045007079,
            "width": 0.40825190010857765,
            "height": 0.04530201342281879
          },
          "block_content": "B ( ν ) and A ( ν ) are summarized over the science band and science core using medians, percentiles, or simple channel- wise sums, depending on the diagnostic being performed.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "u5TRxNOeci",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08143322475570032,
            "y": 0.05234898816819159,
            "width": 0.011943539630836048,
            "height": 0.013422818791946308
          },
          "block_content": "4",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "fE2tQ_ONTL",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.48642779587404994,
            "y": 0.05486576669168152,
            "width": 0.03474484256243214,
            "height": 0.013422818791946308
          },
          "block_content": "Kim",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "mH45aSc7Uh",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.5548317046688382,
            "y": 0.08003355192658085,
            "width": 0.32030401737242126,
            "height": 0.018456375838926176
          },
          "block_content": "4.2. Temporally smoothed SVD (TempSVD)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "Lmvcx6X3Bs",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.20521172638436483,
            "y": 0.14043623649033923,
            "width": 0.16395222584147665,
            "height": 0.015939597315436243
          },
          "block_content": "3.3. Auxiliary Metrics",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "vh_ffHQUrS",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08143322475570032,
            "y": 0.16308724320174864,
            "width": 0.41042345276872966,
            "height": 0.044463087248322146
          },
          "block_content": "To connect Monte Carlo summaries to scientific impact, we use two additional aggregate metrics. First, we define the integrated absolute error over the science core as",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "ltR1cxntUY",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.50814332247557,
            "y": 0.10268455863799025,
            "width": 0.41259500542888167,
            "height": 0.10822147651006711
          },
          "block_content": "To benchmark the effect of imposing temporal regularity on the fitted low-rank component, we include a simple temporally smoothed SVD reference method. Let K ∈ R T × T be a linear smoothing operator acting along time (we use a symmetric boxcar moving-average window of width m samples, normalized to unit row sum). We form the smoothed matrix",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "0C5XND_QfD",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08251900108577633,
            "y": 0.2595637596693615,
            "width": 0.40933767643865365,
            "height": 0.044463087248322146
          },
          "block_content": "which serves as a channel-summed proxy (i.e., a discrete sum over channels, with no explicit ∆ ν factor) within the protected region.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "4wG__j54Ug",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.09337676438653637,
            "y": 0.3057046992666769,
            "width": 0.3322475570032573,
            "height": 0.014261744966442953
          },
          "block_content": "Second, we define the detection failure rate as",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "0joV_5jKJ4",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.47014115092290987,
            "y": 0.3359060403484626,
            "width": 0.019543973941368076,
            "height": 0.015939597315436243
          },
          "block_content": "(8)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "Nt9rQ1MxMt",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08360477741585233,
            "y": 0.37114094087741517,
            "width": 0.40825190010857765,
            "height": 0.10654362416107382
          },
          "block_content": "where N trial is the total number of injection–recovery tri- als and N fail is the number of trials in which a Gaussian line fit to the recovered spectrum within the science core either fails to converge or yields a fitted amplitude below the adopted detection threshold. This metric quantifies missed recovery of the injected science feature rather than generic spectral-shape errors.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "yJI6bxt9V5",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.510314875135722,
            "y": 0.259563758469268,
            "width": 0.40933767643865365,
            "height": 0.04278523489932886
          },
          "block_content": "compute its rank- k truncated-SVD approximation ( D (sm) ) k , and subtract this fit from the original (un- smoothed) snapshot,",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "fRc2U1Swzj",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.23127035830618892,
            "y": 0.4911073902309341,
            "width": 0.10857763300760044,
            "height": 0.013422818791946308
          },
          "block_content": "4. METHODS",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "4ppfe2R88G",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08251900108577633,
            "y": 0.511241605617856,
            "width": 0.40933767643865365,
            "height": 0.044463087248322146
          },
          "block_content": "We now define the low-rank cleaning methods consid- ered for a single-epoch matrix D ∈ R T × F and the com- parison references.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "p0KxF_6ixB",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.13897937024972856,
            "y": 0.5699664378326211,
            "width": 0.2953311617806732,
            "height": 0.015100671140939598
          },
          "block_content": "4.1. Frequency-weighted SVD (FWSVD)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "2mIoGFKkXA",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08143322475570032,
            "y": 0.5892617398460439,
            "width": 0.40825190010857765,
            "height": 0.04697986577181208
          },
          "block_content": "To suppress variance explanation in the protected chan- nels, we introduce a diagonal weight matrix W ∈ R F × F along the frequency axis. Channel weights are",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "I9t5hTea4V",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.510314875135722,
            "y": 0.34765100799150916,
            "width": 0.40933767643865365,
            "height": 0.07885906040268456
          },
          "block_content": "The window width m controls the strength of temporal averaging: larger m suppresses fast time variability but can introduce horizontal (time-smeared) residual struc- ture. We treat TempSVD as an illustrative regularized reference method, not as a proposed default.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "DG6zMDHsGP",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.510314875135722,
            "y": 0.42986577949267907,
            "width": 0.40716612377850164,
            "height": 0.05956375838926174
          },
          "block_content": "In practice, for TempSVD we use an alternating least- squares solver for the rank-1 case for numerical stabil- ity and computational efficiency, while retaining the same conceptual structure.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "riq8DTJPRd",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.510314875135722,
            "y": 0.4927852425799274,
            "width": 0.40933767643865365,
            "height": 0.0738255033557047
          },
          "block_content": "To summarize the trade-off between science distortion and residual RFI contamination, we define two scalar Pareto proxies over the science band. For clarity, ‘residual RFI contamination’ denotes signal remaining after clean- ing, not instrumental spectral leakage or ADC artifacts.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "v6KUeimSw9",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.5233441910966341,
            "y": 0.5682885854836278,
            "width": 0.20629750271444083,
            "height": 0.015100671140939598
          },
          "block_content": "The science-distortion proxy,",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "xmoqNWPvQV",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.6156351791530941,
            "y": 0.5942952968930238,
            "width": 0.20086862106406078,
            "height": 0.03942953020134228
          },
          "block_content": "  \\mathrm{Bias}^{-}\n  =\n  1 -\n  \\frac{\\sum_{\\nu \\in \\mathrm{band}} \\hat{S}(\\nu)}{\\sum_{\\nu \\in \\mathrm{band}} S(\\nu)} ,",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "opSq-1UxAx",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.511400651465798,
            "y": 0.6471476458863124,
            "width": 0.40716612377850164,
            "height": 0.08976510067114093
          },
          "block_content": "measures the signed fractional change of the injected sci- ence component after cleaning (Bias − = 0 for perfect preservation). Negative values correspond to net ampli- fication rather than loss. In Pareto plots we therefore use | Bias − | as a distortion magnitude, while retaining the sign in tabulated summaries.",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "AKeld-hOPl",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.5255157437567861,
            "y": 0.7369127465574533,
            "width": 0.247557003257329,
            "height": 0.015100671140939598
          },
          "block_content": "The residual-contamination proxy,",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "FpeKOkQ3p2",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.6330076004343105,
            "y": 0.7629194579668493,
            "width": 0.16612377850162866,
            "height": 0.03859060402684564
          },
          "block_content": "  \\mathrm{Bias}^{+}\n  =\n  \\frac{\\sum_{\\nu \\in \\mathrm{band}} \\hat{I}(\\nu)}{\\sum_{\\nu \\in \\mathrm{band}} I(\\nu)} ,",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "Dii23ACVkN",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.8892508143322475,
            "y": 0.7738254982353057,
            "width": 0.02823018458197611,
            "height": 0.01761744966442953
          },
          "block_content": "(16)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "2tjtOL-x7d",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.509229098805646,
            "y": 0.8149329063876364,
            "width": 0.41042345276872966,
            "height": 0.0964765100671141
          },
          "block_content": "is evaluated using dedicated RFI-only trials in which the science component is set to S = 0, so that D = I + N . In these trials, the time-averaged residual ˆ I ( ν ) = D ( k ) clean ( t, ν ) t directly estimates the residual RFI contam- ination that survives rank- k subtraction. The denomina- tor P ν ∈ band I ( ν ) is the corresponding time-average of the",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "IQpSRsbJvV",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08251900108577633,
            "y": 0.7268456324634937,
            "width": 0.41042345276872966,
            "height": 0.026845637583892617
          },
          "block_content": "with 0 < w core ≤ w prot ≤ 1, and W = diag  w ( ν ) \u0001 . We define the frequency-weighted snapshot as",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "tXW8YWpBvn",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08251900108577633,
            "y": 0.7956376043742135,
            "width": 0.16069489685124863,
            "height": 0.012583892617449664
          },
          "block_content": "and compute its SVD,",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "maIAJ08FIZ",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.08034744842562432,
            "y": 0.8493288795419988,
            "width": 0.41150922909880566,
            "height": 0.028523489932885907
          },
          "block_content": "For rank k , the rank- k approximation in the weighted space is ˜ U 1: k ˜ Σ 1: k ˜ V ⊤ 1: k , and we subtract",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "FXKRlmkm0n",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.1465798045602606,
            "y": 0.8895973359178376,
            "width": 0.28338762214983715,
            "height": 0.02181208053691275
          },
          "block_content": "D_{\\mathrm{clean}}^{\\mathrm{(FWSVD)}}(k)\n    = D - \\tilde{U}_{1:k} \\ilde{\\Sigma}_{1:k} \\tilde{V}_{1:k}^\\top W^{-1}.",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "i4b3VCmg-4",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.23778501628664495,
            "y": 0.7662751626648359,
            "width": 0.0998914223669924,
            "height": 0.015939597315436344
          },
          "block_content": "D^{(W)} \\equiv D\\,W,",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "ybgKGrQsg2",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.23127035830618892,
            "y": 0.8191275116581245,
            "width": 0.11183496199782844,
            "height": 0.01761744966442953
          },
          "block_content": "D^{(W)} \\approx \\tilde{U} \\tilde{\\Sigma} \\tilde{V}^\\top .",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "KvB99B4rzH",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.4603691639522258,
            "y": 0.7671140888393325,
            "width": 0.029315960912052116,
            "height": 0.014261744966442953
          },
          "block_content": "(10)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "m9DGAkGyo9",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.46145494028230183,
            "y": 0.8199664378326211,
            "width": 0.029315960912052116,
            "height": 0.015100671140939598
          },
          "block_content": "(11)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "--dxJlCC81",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.46145494028230183,
            "y": 0.8929530406158243,
            "width": 0.02823018458197611,
            "height": 0.015100671140939598
          },
          "block_content": "(12)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "Bx2KILCW1I",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.46905537459283386,
            "y": 0.6714765049467151,
            "width": 0.021715526601520086,
            "height": 0.015100671140939598
          },
          "block_content": "(9)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "_owXMLNCkY",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.13355048859934848,
            "y": 0.6479865720608091,
            "width": 0.30184581976112895,
            "height": 0.06291946308724825
          },
          "block_content": "    w_{\\mathrm{core}}, & \\nu \\in \\mathrm{science~core}, \\\\\n    w_{\\mathrm{prot}}, & \\nu \\in \\mathrm{science~band}\\setminus\\mathrm{core}, \\\\\n    1,                 & \\text{otherwise},\n",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "s9BRtcOr0H",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.17698154180238868,
            "y": 0.21593959219503722,
            "width": 0.22041259500542887,
            "height": 0.0327181208053691
          },
          "block_content": "\\mathrm{IAE}_{\\mathrm{core}} =\n\\sum_{\\nu \\in \\mathrm{core}}\n\\bigl|\\hat{S}(\\nu) - S(\\nu)\\bigr|,\n\\label{eq:iae-core}",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "HLhC72R0PP",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.6634093376764386,
            "y": 0.22600670628899697,
            "width": 0.10097719869706841,
            "height": 0.01677852348993288
          },
          "block_content": "D^{(\\mathrm{sm})} = K D,",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "b6t5JOhf7q",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.23561346362649294,
            "y": 0.3317114094759794,
            "width": 0.10097719869706841,
            "height": 0.02936241610738255
          },
          "block_content": "p_{\\mathrm{fail}} = \\frac{N_{\\mathrm{fail}}}{N_{\\mathrm{trial}}},",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "bq6a2UbIUi",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.5982627578718784,
            "y": 0.31409395981154975,
            "width": 0.23127035830618867,
            "height": 0.02181208053691275
          },
          "block_content": "D_{\\mathrm{clean}}^{(\\mathrm{TempSVD})}(k) = D - (D^{(\\mathrm{sm})})_k .",
          "label": "Formula"
        },
        {
          "id": "lRNc84n8XD",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.8892508143322475,
            "y": 0.22432885914040893,
            "width": 0.029315960912052116,
            "height": 0.018456375838926176
          },
          "block_content": "(13)",
          "label": "Text"
        },
        {
          "id": "zWZuOx6emT",
          "order": null,
          "bounding_box": {
            "x": 0.8903365906623235,
            "y": 0.3182885906840331,
            "width": 0.02823018458197611,
            "height": 0.015939597315436243
          },
          "block_content": "(14)",
          "label": "Text"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
